\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Thank you for providing the scoring context and clear ethical boundaries. I will treat this profile as a 
\f1\b private self-reflection snapshot
\f0\b0 , not a diagnosis, fixed identity, or objective assessment of how others experience your leadership.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa348\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs42 \cf0 Executive interpretation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 Your profile suggests a potentially productive but important tension:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 You report 
\f1\b strong humility and ethical leadership
\f0\b0 , which can support openness, fairness, accountability, and responsible use of authority.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 You also report 
\f1\b moderate signals across all four interpersonal risk dimensions
\f0\b0 , most notably around strategic influence and information management.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Your empathy score sits near the upper end of the emerging-capacity band, suggesting a meaningful foundation that may be less consistently accessible under pressure, conflict, fatigue, or time constraints.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf0 One plausible interpretation is that you may see yourself as principled, teachable, and willing to act responsibly while also sometimes becoming more guarded, calculating, image-conscious, blunt, or punitive when stakes rise. That is a hypothesis to test against observable behaviour, not a conclusion about you.\
The central development opportunity is therefore not to reshape your personality. It is to establish safeguards that help your reported ethical intentions remain visible in your conduct when you face criticism, competition, uncertainty, resistance, or perceived unfairness.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa375\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs56 \cf0 1. Balanced interpretation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa348\partightenfactor0

\fs42 \cf0 Likely leadership style\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 This combination could be consistent with a leader who:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Values integrity, fairness, competence, and accountability.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Is willing to learn, acknowledge uncertainty, and give others responsibility.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Thinks strategically about stakeholders, incentives, timing, and influence.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Can make difficult decisions without becoming immobilised by discomfort.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 May prefer purposeful, outcome-oriented communication over extended emotional processing.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 May become more controlling, selective, defensive, or sharp when credibility, status, control, or delivery is threatened.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Your 
\f1\b humility score of 82
\f0\b0  is an important reported strength. It suggests that admitting uncertainty, learning from others, giving credit, and acknowledging mistakes may already be part of your leadership repertoire. This could help regulate the moderate narcissism signal by making it easier to separate correction from personal rejection.\
Your 
\f1\b ethical leadership score of 79
\f0\b0  suggests a strong stated commitment to fairness, transparency, confidentiality, and safe challenge. This can provide a useful internal standard for regulating strategic influence, shortcuts, retaliation, and disproportionate responses.\
Your 
\f1\b empathy score of 64
\f0\b0  is close to the reported-strength threshold but remains an emerging capacity under the tool\'92s bands. You may understand others\'92 perspectives reasonably well while still benefiting from more consistent pauses to examine emotional and relational impact, especially when a decision feels urgent or obvious to you.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa348\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs42 \cf0 Possible biases to examine\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 These are possibilities for reflection, not claims that you display them.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 1. Outcome-over-process bias\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 When a goal appears legitimate or urgent, you may be more willing to justify selective communication, forceful influence, or procedural shortcuts. The question to monitor is not only, \'93Is my desired outcome good?\'94 but also, \'93Is the way I am pursuing it fair, transparent, and acceptable if made visible?\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 2. Competence and intent bias\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 Because you report strong humility and ethics, you may occasionally give your own conduct the benefit of good intentions while evaluating others more heavily by impact or performance. A useful corrective is to evaluate your actions by both intent and observable effect.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 3. Threat sensitivity around recognition or criticism\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 The moderate narcissism signal may become more visible when your expertise, contribution, authority, or public image feels challenged. Possible behavioural expressions include explaining too quickly, redirecting attention toward your contribution, discounting the source of criticism, or becoming preoccupied with how the situation looks.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 4. Strategic information bias\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 The Machiavellianism score is your highest dark reflective signal. This does not indicate manipulation as a fact. It does suggest that information control, stakeholder positioning, impression management, or tactical influence deserve particular attention.\
A useful distinction is:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Legitimate discretion:
\f0\b0  Protecting confidentiality, following policy, or sequencing communication responsibly.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Risky selectivity:
\f0\b0  Withholding information mainly to preserve personal advantage, avoid scrutiny, or constrain another person\'92s choices.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 5. Emotional-distance bias\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 Under pressure, you may focus on logic, delivery, or proportionality without fully recognising the emotional consequences for others. This could make a response feel efficient or justified to you but intimidating, humiliating, or dismissive to someone with less power.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa348\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs42 \cf0 Workplace triggers worth monitoring\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 Your risk signals may be more likely to appear in situations involving:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Public criticism or questioning of your expertise.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Competition for recognition, resources, promotion, or influence.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Resistance from someone you believe should comply.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A perceived breach of loyalty or confidentiality.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Time pressure, fatigue, or high-stakes delivery.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Repeated underperformance by another person.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Organisational politics or ambiguous decision rights.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Situations where you believe another person has acted unfairly.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Humour or informal exchanges where status differences are present.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Environments that reward results while neglecting respectful process.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa348\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs42 \cf0 Context-sensitive risk points\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 Power asymmetry\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 Bluntness or humour that feels harmless among peers may feel coercive or humiliating to a student, junior colleague, direct report, or someone dependent on your evaluation.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 Private versus public settings\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 Corrective feedback delivered publicly can create unnecessary social defeat even when the underlying concern is valid. Private, specific, proportionate feedback is generally safer.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 High urgency\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 Urgency can narrow consequence-checking. A short pause becomes especially valuable when a decision affects reputation, workload, access to information, or career opportunity.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 Organisational ambiguity\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 When roles or rules are unclear, strategic information management can gradually become unfair gatekeeping. Written decision criteria and documented responsibilities can reduce this risk.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 Moral certainty\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 Strong ethical self-confidence can sometimes create a blind spot: \'93Because my aim is ethical, my method must also be ethical.\'94 Your humility can help counter this by inviting challenge about both means and ends.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
