\f1\b\fs56 \cf0 5. Short workplace scripts\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa348\partightenfactor0

\fs42 \cf0 Seeking feedback\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 Direct version\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 \'93I am working on making it safer for people to disagree with me. Thinking about our recent meetings, what is one behaviour I should continue and one I should change?\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 Lower-pressure version\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 \'93You do not need to answer immediately. When you have time, I would value one specific example of where my communication helped discussion and one where I may have closed it down.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 When feedback is difficult to hear\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 \'93I notice I want to explain myself, but I would rather understand first. Could you give me a specific example and describe the impact?\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa348\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs42 \cf0 Pausing before a reactive decision\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 \'93This matters, and I do not want urgency to produce an avoidable mistake. I am going to pause, check the consequences and relevant policy, and respond by [time].\'94\
For a meeting:\
\'93I have an immediate reaction, but I do not want to treat it as a considered decision. Let me ask two clarifying questions before I respond.\'94\
For written communication:\
\'93I have received this. I want to consider the facts and potential impact before replying substantively.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa348\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs42 \cf0 Giving credit\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 \'93I want to be specific about attribution. The original insight came from [name], and [name] translated it into the approach we are using.\'94\
\'93I presented the recommendation, but it reflects substantial work by [names or team]. Their analysis changed the final decision.\'94\
\'93I was credited for this earlier, but the contribution was shared. In particular, [name] identified the issue and [name] developed the solution.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa348\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs42 \cf0 Repairing harm\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 \'93My wording in that conversation was sharper than necessary, and I can see that it may have undermined you. The concern itself still needs discussion, but I should have raised it privately and respectfully. I am sorry. I will handle that differently.\'94\
\'93I interrupted and dismissed your point before understanding it. That was not fair. If you are willing, I would like to hear the point again without defending my earlier response.\'94\
A sound repair should:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls27\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Name your behaviour.\
\ls27\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Recognise likely impact without dictating how the other person feels.\
\ls27\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Avoid turning the apology into a defence.\
\ls27\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 State the behavioural change.\
\ls27\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Respect that forgiveness or reassurance may not be immediate.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa348\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs42 \cf0 Responding ethically to conflict\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 \'93We appear to disagree about both the facts and the next step. Let us separate those. I will explain the evidence and criteria I am using, then I would like to hear what you believe I have missed.\'94\
\'93I want to address the work issue without making assumptions about your motives. The behaviour I observed was [specific behaviour], and the impact was [specific impact]. What is your perspective?\'94\
\'93I am too frustrated to handle this constructively right now. I am going to pause rather than say something disproportionate. We can resume at [specific time].\'94\
If the issue may involve serious misconduct:\
\'93This may require formal handling rather than an informal resolution. I will preserve confidentiality, avoid making premature conclusions, and use the appropriate organisational process.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
